On Sun, 30 Jul 2006, L wrote:
>
>> 14: #dragging corpses that are too heavy to lift.  (Use some of the
>> iron ball mechanics for this, perhaps.)
>
> Why not drag any item which is too massive? Or, why not _push_ any item
> which is too massive? This intrigues me yet it seems to require not
> insignificant amounts of coding.

   One way to do it which might require less coding, and no major
interface changes, would be to allow the player to (a)pply a leash
to a corpse and then just start moving, dragging the corpse along
behind.

   (If your pet dies while leashed, does the leash fall off its neck
by magic? Or can you already drag dead things around?)

   But dragging a big heavy corpse requires almost as much strength
as simply lifting it in the first place --- maybe more, depending on
surface area --- so this YANI isn't realistic. And all it does is
reward careless players who kill dragons on top of thrones, two steps
from the altar, or whatever. Killing things in the right place at the
right time is part of the game; removing it serves no purpose.

